nodes.body:
@TheDuyIT, thank you for your PR.

I believe we cannot continue with this approach. First of all, I am worry about the size of vllm/parser/llama_json.py. Is's over **1.5 KLOC**. Compare for example parsers for other models like qwen, deepseek, inkling. All of them no more that several hundreds of lines, but definitely not thousands. As a consequence of this large size is that it would be quite impossible to maintain this code. Secondly, I spent today about several hours trying to understand the architecture of this change and reproduce BFCL but wasn't able to progress in that. So, I believe change is really not intuitive and simple in a way, we definitely need to do something with that.

To give you some ideas to action, I would suggest to start from writing **manually** short and clear description first that would explain what your change is trying to achieve and architecture of implemented idea. Then implement from scratch llama parser following architecture of already existing parsers for other models in vllm/parser.

